 "$comment": "AEP-0002 Annex A machine-usable fixture for the VS Code agent OTel-inbound channel (design record: the spec repo docs/components/bridge-otlp-inbound-design.md, the second-vendor profile decision). Each entry pins the pure record->event mapping over FLATTENED attributes at the default metadata ceiling, in BOTH modes: companion (the default \u2014 everything in the channel-visible x.vscode.otel.* family, core types never emitted; the hook adapter stays the sole core-type authority) and primary (hook-less deployments \u2014 the core subset: the session frame plus tool-call outcomes; the hook decision tier never reaches this channel, so tool.denied is NEVER emitted here, and session end does not exist on this vendor surface, so session.ended is never synthesized). Resource/attribute keys follow the vendor source read at the pinned tag; values are representative and refined at live validation. Envelope identity (resource session.id -> session, agent vscode, no runs synthesized) is receiver wiring, pinned by the reference smoke.",
